From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:25:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] zink: fix lost-wakeup deadlock in the multi-context
 unflushed-batch wait

Three bugs in one path:
  - usage.unflushed cleared without the mutex held
  - cnd_broadcast issued un-mutexed
  - the waiter neither loops nor rechecks its predicate, and its timedwait uses an
    epoch-absolute {0, 10000} timespec, so the trywait has never actually waited

A clear that lands between the waiter's unlocked check and its cnd_wait is a lost wakeup, and
the waiter then sleeps forever on a signal that already fired.

This was in the guest series as patches/mesa 0014 and was dropped on 2026-08-04 with the rest
of the zink rows, because guest GL stopped riding zink and moved to virgl/vrend. That is true
of the SESSION, and not of everything: venus_replay drives zink inside the guest on purpose,
as the vehicle for exercising venus offscreen through eglretrace, so the guest kept running
this code with the fix removed from under it. It comes back for that reason.

Not reproduced under this build: the reasoning is that the hang the fix addresses was
root-caused in exactly this test, that the code here is the unfixed shape byte for byte, and
that venus_replay currently wedges until the harness's 900 s ssh cap where it normally takes
~90 s. The host build has carried the fix since 47308c0f026.

Forensics: spikes/venus-replay-zink-hang-2026-07-12/RESULTS.md, which root-causes the wedge by
reading unflushed == 0 out of the blocked process and waking it by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 47308c0f026bbe2c5bb8efa8316d64355b6431e8)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
index c4e5ee3698b..6c5c4a68f3b 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
@@ -653,9 +653,17 @@ submit_queue(void *data, void *gdata, int thread_index)
    int num_si = ZINK_SUBMIT_MAX;
    while (!bs->fence.batch_id)
       bs->fence.batch_id = (uint32_t)p_atomic_inc_return(&screen->curr_batch);
+   /* the unflushed clear must happen under the usage mutex: waiters in
+    * zink_batch_usage_unflushed_wait() check the flag under that mutex before
+    * sleeping on u->flush, and a clear that lands between an unlocked check and
+    * the cnd_wait is a lost wakeup (observed as an infinite sleep on u->flush
+    * with every flush queue idle)
+    */
+   mtx_lock(&bs->usage.mtx);
    bs->usage.usage = bs->fence.batch_id;
    assert(bs->usage.usage);
    bs->usage.unflushed = false;
+   mtx_unlock(&bs->usage.mtx);
 
    uint64_t batch_id = bs->fence.batch_id;
    /* first submit is just for acquire waits since they have a separate array */
@@ -844,7 +852,12 @@ submit_queue(void *data, void *gdata, int thread_index)
 
    bs->usage.submit_count++;
 end:
+   /* broadcast under the mutex so the wake can't slip between a waiter's locked
+    * predicate check and its cnd_wait
+    */
+   mtx_lock(&bs->usage.mtx);
    cnd_broadcast(&bs->usage.flush);
+   mtx_unlock(&bs->usage.mtx);
 
    post_submit(bs, screen);
 
@@ -1206,12 +1219,30 @@ zink_batch_usage_unflushed_wait(struct zink_context *ctx, struct zink_batch_usag
          ctx->base.flush(&ctx->base, NULL, PIPE_FLUSH_HINT_FINISH);
          return true;
       } else { //multi-context
+         /* re-check the predicate under the mutex and wait in a loop: the submit
+          * thread clears `unflushed` and broadcasts `flush` under this same mutex,
+          * so a checked-then-wait without the re-check races the broadcast and
+          * sleeps forever on a signal that already fired
+          */
          mtx_lock(&u->mtx);
          if (trywait) {
-            struct timespec ts = {0, 10000};
-            cnd_timedwait(&u->flush, &u->mtx, &ts);
-         } else
-            cnd_wait(&u->flush, &u->mtx);
+            if (u->unflushed) {
+               /* cnd_timedwait takes an ABSOLUTE TIME_UTC timespec; the previous
+                * {0, 10000} was epoch+10us, i.e. always already expired
+                */
+               struct timespec ts;
+               timespec_get(&ts, TIME_UTC);
+               ts.tv_nsec += 10000;
+               if (ts.tv_nsec >= 1000000000) {
+                  ts.tv_sec++;
+                  ts.tv_nsec -= 1000000000;
+               }
+               cnd_timedwait(&u->flush, &u->mtx, &ts);
+            }
+         } else {
+            while (u->unflushed)
+               cnd_wait(&u->flush, &u->mtx);
+         }
          mtx_unlock(&u->mtx);
       }
    }
